---@class growthbook.Config
---@field id string
---@field key string Stable reference handle; used as `@config:key` in values
---@field name string
---@field owner? string The userId of the owner (or raw owner name/email for legacy records)
---@field ownerEmail? string The email address of the owner, when the owner can be resolved to a known user.
---@field parent? string The `key` of the config this one inherits from (lineage parent — the primary spine). Synthesized into `$extends` at resolution time and never stored in `value`.
---@field extends? growthbook.ConfigExtendsList Additional composition bases (config `key`s) layered on top of `parent`, in precedence order (later overrides earlier; all override `parent`; this config's own keys win last). Like `parent`, set via this field — never via a `@config:` entry in `value`.
---@field value? growthbook.ConfigValueMap This config's own base value as a JSON object (its declared fields only — inherited fields are layered in at resolution time, not stored here). Per-environment/project variants are expressed via `scopedOverrides`, not here.
---@field scopedOverrides? growthbook.ConfigScopedOverridesList Ordered, first-match-wins environment/project-scoped variant selection. Each entry points at a flavor config (a child config, by `key`) whose value is deep-merged onto this config's resolved value when the (environment, project) scope matches — resolved at build time, per layer. This is how you create an environment-scoped override (as opposed to a plain child config): make a child config for the override value, then add it here with its scope. Send the complete list to replace it; an empty array clears all overrides. Entries must reference existing configs, may not reference this config itself, and may not be unreachable (fully subsumed by an earlier entry).
---@field scopedConfig? growthbook.ConfigScopedConfig Present ONLY when this config is an environment/project-scoped override (a "flavor") of another config. Its value is a patch that applies solely within the listed environments/projects, layered onto `parent` at resolution — it is NOT a standalone config. A plain config (including an ordinary child that just inherits from a `parent`) omits this field entirely. Read-only: create/change the relationship via the parent config's `scopedOverrides`, never by setting this directly.
---@field description? string
---@field project? string The project this config belongs to (empty = all projects)
---@field archived? boolean
---@field schema? growthbook.ConfigSchema This config's own field definitions as a JSON Schema document (its contribution to the family's effective schema). Inherited fields are owned by ancestors and are not repeated here.
---@field extensible? boolean Whether this config family permits extra keys beyond the declared fields (child configs, feature rules, ad-hoc overrides). Only the root config's flag applies. Absent = inherit the org default.
---@field invariants? growthbook.ConfigInvariantsList Cross-field validation rules (relational checks JSON Schema can't express, e.g. implications or comparing two fields), evaluated against the resolved value at publish.
---@field locked? boolean Whether this Config is locked to a published revision. Drafts can still be created and edited while locked, but no change can be published until a user with Bypass draft approvals access unlocks it.
---@field experimentGuard? boolean Whether the experiment guard is enabled. When enabled, publishing a value used by a running experiment returns a warning that must be acknowledged with `ignoreWarnings: true`. Disabling the guard requires Bypass draft approvals access.
---@field lockedRevision? growthbook.ConfigLockedRevision The pinned published revision (present only when `locked`). Fetch it via `GET /configs-revisions/:key/:version` for a value guaranteed not to disappear or mutate — use it to pin reproducible builds.
---@field lockedBy? string Who locked the config: a member's user ID, or an API key's ID when it acted as itself
---@field dateLocked? string When the config was locked (when `locked`).
---@field dateCreated string
---@field dateUpdated string

---Additional composition bases (config `key`s) layered on top of `parent`, in precedence order (later overrides earlier; all override `parent`; this config's own keys win last). Like `parent`, set via this field — never via a `@config:` entry in `value`.
---@alias growthbook.ConfigExtendsList string[]

