---@class growthbook.CreateExperimentRequest
---@field datasourceId? string ID for the [DataSource](#tag/DataSource_model). Can only be set if a templateId is not provided.
---@field assignmentQuery? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestAssignmentQuery The assignment query, grouping its ID with the identifier type analyzed on. Mutually exclusive with the deprecated `assignmentQueryId`. Can only be set if a templateId is not provided.
---@field assignmentQueryId? string Deprecated: use `assignmentQuery`. Rejected when selecting a different assignment query that declares several identifier types; set `assignmentQuery.identifierType` instead. Can only be set if a templateId is not provided.
---@field isClusterExperiment? boolean Run as a cluster-randomized experiment: randomize on the assignment query's identifier type (the cluster, e.g. region_id) while analyzing a nested sub-unit (clusterSubUnitIdentifier, e.g. user_id). The assignment query must declare both identifier types.
---@field clusterSubUnitIdentifier? string The nested sub-unit identifier type analyzed within each cluster (e.g. user_id). Required when isClusterExperiment is true; must be declared by the assignment query and differ from its cluster identifier type.
---@field trackingKey string Key sent with exposure events. Keep it short, in kebab-case (usually the Feature Flag key). If your organization requires a tracking key format, a key that doesn't match is rejected with `invalid_tracking_key`. Changing it after launch splits exposures across two keys.
---@field bypassDuplicateKeyCheck? boolean If true, allow creating an experiment even if another experiment with the same tracking key already exists. This is ignored if the organization requires unique tracking keys as a rule. Only set this when a person has explicitly asked you to. If a check blocks you, stop and ask a person instead of working around it.
---@field name string Short display name (e.g. `Express checkout button`). Put reasoning in `hypothesis` and context in `description`.
---@field type? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestType|string
---@field project? string Project ID which the experiment belongs to
---@field templateId? string ID of the [ExperimentTemplate](#tag/ExperimentTemplate_model) this experiment was created from. Template fields are applied by default and overridden by explicitly provided payload fields.
---@field hypothesis? string Markdown. If we change X, metric Y will move because Z.
---@field description? string Markdown. Put context here, not in the name.
---@field tags? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestTagsList Tags for filtering and grouping. Use these instead of encoding groups in names.
---@field metrics? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestMetricsList
---@field secondaryMetrics? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestSecondaryMetricsList
---@field guardrailMetrics? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestGuardrailMetricsList
---@field activationMetric? string Users must convert on this metric before being included
---@field segmentId? string Only users in this segment will be included
---@field queryFilter? string WHERE clause to add to the default experiment query
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization. When omitted, it defaults to the requesting member: a personal access token's owner, or the member an organization API key assumes. An organization API key acting as itself leaves it empty.
---@field archived? boolean
---@field status? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestStatus|string
---@field autoRefresh? boolean
---@field hashAttribute? string
---@field fallbackAttribute? string
---@field attributeScopeAllProjects? boolean Picker preference: show attributes from all projects in this experiment's targeting UI instead of only those in scope for its project and linked features. Does not loosen enforcement — when the organization requires registered attributes with project scoping, out-of-scope attributes are still rejected.
---@field hashVersion? number
---@field disableStickyBucketing? boolean When true, disables Sticky Bucketing for this experiment. If omitted, defaults to your organization's Sticky Bucketing setting for new experiments. Sticky Bucketing only takes effect when it is also enabled at the organization level.
---@field bucketVersion? number
---@field minBucketVersion? number
---@field releasedVariationId? string
---@field excludeFromPayload? boolean
---@field inProgressConversions? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestInProgressConversions|string
---@field attributionModel? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestAttributionModel|string Setting attribution model to `"experimentDuration"` is the same as selecting "Ignore Conversion Windows" for the Conversion Window Override. Setting it to `"lookbackOverride"` requires a `lookbackOverride` object to be provided.
---@field lookbackOverride? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestLookbackOverride Controls the lookback override for the experiment. For type "window", value must be a non-negative number and valueUnit is required.
---@field statsEngine? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestStatsEngine|string
---@field variations growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestVariationsList
---@field phases? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestPhasesList
---@field regressionAdjustmentEnabled? boolean Controls whether regression adjustment (CUPED) is enabled for experiment analyses
---@field sequentialTestingEnabled? boolean Only applicable to frequentist analyses
---@field sequentialTestingTuningParameter? number
---@field shareLevel? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestShareLevel|string
---@field banditScheduleValue? number
---@field banditScheduleUnit? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestBanditScheduleUnit|string
---@field banditBurnInValue? number
---@field banditBurnInUnit? growthbook.CreateExperimentRequestBanditBurnInUnit|string
