---@class growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2
---@field id string Stable revision id. Newer revisions carry opaque ids; older ones a derived `frev_<version>_<featureId>` form. Both work wherever revision ids are accepted.
---@field featureId string The feature this revision belongs to
---@field baseVersion number
---@field version number
---@field comment string
---@field date string
---@field status string
---@field createdBy? growthbook.EventUser
---@field publishedBy? growthbook.EventUser
---@field defaultValue? string The default value at the time this revision was created. When the feature is in Config mode, this is the JSON override patch merged on top of the config (its own keys win); otherwise it is the full value.
---@field defaultValueConfig? string|distilled.Null Optional. A config within `baseConfig`'s family that the default value resolves to instead of `baseConfig` itself. null or omitted means the default is `baseConfig`. The default is exactly this config and carries no overrides of its own.
---@field rules growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2RulesList Unified rules array. Each rule carries its own environment scope via `allEnvironments` / `environments`.
---@field definitions? growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2DefinitionsMap
---@field environmentsEnabled? growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2EnvironmentsEnabledMap Per-environment enabled state captured in this revision (only present when kill-switch gating is enabled)
---@field envPrerequisites? growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2EnvPrerequisitesMap Per-environment prerequisites captured in this revision (only present when prerequisite gating is enabled)
---@field prerequisites? growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2PrerequisitesList Feature-level prerequisites captured in this revision. Each entry is a boolean flag ID that must evaluate to true for this flag to be active for a given user.
---@field metadata? growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2Metadata Metadata fields captured in this revision (only present when metadata gating is enabled)
---@field rampActions? growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2RampActionsList Pending ramp schedule actions that will be applied when this draft is published
---@field autoPublishOnApproval? boolean When true, the revision is armed to publish automatically once governance allows (immediately on approval, or on `scheduledPublishAt` if set).
---@field scheduledPublishAt? string|distilled.Null Target date for a deferred (scheduled) publish. Null/absent means publish as soon as approved.
---@field scheduledPublishLockEdits? boolean When true, content edits to this draft are frozen while the schedule is pending (rebasing is still allowed).
---@field scheduledPublishLockOthers? boolean When true, publishing other drafts of this feature is blocked while the schedule is pending.
---@field scheduledPublishBypassApproval? boolean Whether the schedule was created for an unapproved draft by a caller with Bypass draft approvals access. This kind of schedule cannot be edited; cancel it and create a new schedule instead. Anyone with Publish access can cancel it.
---@field scheduledPublishLastError? string Set when a due scheduled publish keeps failing (e.g. still awaiting approval, merge conflict). Indicates the schedule is stuck and retrying.
---@field autoPublishEnabledBy? string User or API key the deferred publish runs as, re-checked when it fires. A key that assumed a member's role is recorded as `<keyId>:<memberId>`.
---@field autoPublishEnabledByUser? growthbook.EventUser Who armed the deferred publish, with an API key's name
---@field scheduledPublishAttempts? number How many times the poller has tried to publish this revision. Read with `scheduledPublishGaveUpAt` to tell a schedule that is still retrying from one that has been parked.
---@field scheduledPublishGaveUpAt? string When the poller stopped retrying. Giving up CLEARS the schedule and disarms auto-publish, so nothing fires again until the revision is re-armed. The draft is left open, with `scheduledPublishLastError` preserved for context.
---@field reviews? growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2ReviewsList Reviewer verdicts for the current review cycle (one entry per reviewer). Verdicts flip to their -stale variants when draft content changes after submission; the list is cleared when a new review cycle starts. Absent on revisions that predate this field.

---@alias growthbook.FeatureRevisionV2DefinitionsMap { [string]: string }

