---Populated when monitoring is enabled and analysis data is available. Contains the current evaluator decision, aggregate traffic health, and per-metric status with effect sizes.
---@class growthbook.HealthSummary
---@field safeToAdvance boolean True only when every hold condition is cleared: the step interval has elapsed, any required approval has been granted, min sample size is met, and all monitored metrics are within bounds. Equivalent to `decision === 'advance'`.
---@field decision growthbook.HealthSummaryDecision Current evaluator decision for the active step. Incorporates all hold conditions (timing, approval, min sample, metric health). When monitoring data is not yet available, the evaluator returns `hold` with a descriptive `decisionReason`.
---@field decisionReason? string Human-readable reason for a hold, rollback, or pause decision.
---@field signals growthbook.HealthSummarySignalsList All active health signals, not just the top-priority one. Useful for surfacing multiple concurrent issues (e.g. SRM + guardrail failing simultaneously). `healthy` is the sole entry when no issues are detected.
---@field snapshotAt? string ISO timestamp of the most recent successful analysis snapshot.
---@field traffic? growthbook.HealthSummaryTraffic Traffic health from the latest snapshot. Absent when no snapshot has been taken yet.
---@field metrics growthbook.HealthSummaryMetricsMap Per-metric health keyed by metric ID. Only includes metrics configured as guardrails or signals on this schedule.

---Current evaluator decision for the active step. Incorporates all hold conditions (timing, approval, min sample, metric health). When monitoring data is not yet available, the evaluator returns `hold` with a descriptive `decisionReason`.
---@alias growthbook.HealthSummaryDecision "advance"|"hold"|"rollback"|"pause"

---Per-metric health keyed by metric ID. Only includes metrics configured as guardrails or signals on this schedule.
---@alias growthbook.HealthSummaryMetricsMap { [string]: growthbook.HealthSummaryMetricsValue }

---@class growthbook.HealthSummaryMetricsValue
---@field id string Metric ID.
---@field name? string Human-readable metric name. Absent if the metric definition has been deleted.
---@field status growthbook.HealthSummaryMetricsValueStatus `failing` = statistically significant regression; `within-bounds` = no significant harm detected; `not-enough-data` = insufficient data to evaluate.
---@field role growthbook.HealthSummaryMetricsValueRole Whether this metric is a guardrail (triggers rollback on loss) or a signal (triggers hold on loss).
---@field relativeLift? number Expected relative lift of the treatment arm vs the baseline arm (e.g. 0.05 = +5%). See `traffic.variationUnits` for what each arm represents.
---@field absoluteLift? number Absolute difference in conversion rate between the treatment and baseline arms.
---@field ciHarmBound? number One-tailed CI bound in the direction of potential harm. For normal metrics (higher is better) this is the lower CI bound; for inverse metrics (lower is better, e.g. errors, latency) this is the upper CI bound. Values further from zero in the harmful direction indicate greater potential regression.
---@field pValue? number Two-sided p-value for the metric effect. Only present when the stats engine produces a frequentist result.

---Whether this metric is a guardrail (triggers rollback on loss) or a signal (triggers hold on loss).
---@alias growthbook.HealthSummaryMetricsValueRole "guardrail"|"signal"

---`failing` = statistically significant regression; `within-bounds` = no significant harm detected; `not-enough-data` = insufficient data to evaluate.
---@alias growthbook.HealthSummaryMetricsValueStatus "failing"|"within-bounds"|"not-enough-data"

---@alias growthbook.HealthSummarySignalsItem "guardrail-failing"|"signal-regression"|"srm"|"multiple-exposures"|"no-traffic"|"below-min-sample"|"healthy"|"awaiting-data"

---All active health signals, not just the top-priority one. Useful for surfacing multiple concurrent issues (e.g. SRM + guardrail failing simultaneously). `healthy` is the sole entry when no issues are detected.
---@alias growthbook.HealthSummarySignalsList growthbook.HealthSummarySignalsItem[]

---Traffic health from the latest snapshot. Absent when no snapshot has been taken yet.
---@class growthbook.HealthSummaryTraffic
---@field totalUsers number Total unique users across all variations.
---@field variationUnits growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficVariationUnitsList Per-variation user counts. Index 0 = baseline arm (users continuing to see the existing behavior — either the configured control value on a v1 safe rollout, or users passed through to subsequent rules / feature default on a v2 monitored ramp). Index 1 = treatment arm (users exposed to the new rollout value).
---@field srm? growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficSrm
---@field multipleExposures? growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficMultipleExposures

---@class growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficMultipleExposures
---@field count number Number of users exposed to both variations.
---@field percent number Fraction of total users with multiple exposures (0–1).
---@field status growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficMultipleExposuresStatus

---@alias growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficMultipleExposuresStatus "ok"|"warning"

---@class growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficSrm
---@field pValue number SRM p-value from the traffic query.
---@field status growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficSrmStatus `failing` when p-value is below the org SRM threshold, indicating a traffic imbalance.

---`failing` when p-value is below the org SRM threshold, indicating a traffic imbalance.
---@alias growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficSrmStatus "ok"|"failing"

---Per-variation user counts. Index 0 = baseline arm (users continuing to see the existing behavior — either the configured control value on a v1 safe rollout, or users passed through to subsequent rules / feature default on a v2 monitored ramp). Index 1 = treatment arm (users exposed to the new rollout value).
---@alias growthbook.HealthSummaryTrafficVariationUnitsList number[]

---@class growthbook.Holdout
---@field id string
