---@class growthbook.PostFactMetricAnalysisRequest
---@field id string The fact metric id to analyze
---@field userIdType? string The identifier type to use for the analysis. If not provided, defaults to the first available identifier type in the fact table.
---@field lookbackDays? number Number of days to look back for the analysis. Defaults to 30.
---@field populationType? growthbook.PostFactMetricAnalysisRequestPopulationType|string The type of population to analyze. Defaults to 'factTable', meaning the analysis will return the metric value for all units found in the fact table.
---@field populationId? string|distilled.Null The ID of the population (e.g., segment ID) when populationType is not 'factTable'. Defaults to null.
---@field additionalNumeratorFilters? growthbook.PostFactMetricAnalysisRequestAdditionalNumeratorFiltersList We support passing in adhoc filters for an analysis that don't live on the metric itself. These are in addition to the metric's filters. To use this, you can pass in an array of Fact Table Filter Ids.
---@field additionalDenominatorFilters? growthbook.PostFactMetricAnalysisRequestAdditionalDenominatorFiltersList We support passing in adhoc filters for an analysis that don't live on the metric itself. These are in addition to the metric's filters. To use this, you can pass in an array of Fact Table Filter Ids.
---@field useCache? boolean Whether to use a cached query if one exists. Defaults to true.

---We support passing in adhoc filters for an analysis that don't live on the metric itself. These are in addition to the metric's filters. To use this, you can pass in an array of Fact Table Filter Ids.
---@alias growthbook.PostFactMetricAnalysisRequestAdditionalDenominatorFiltersList string[]

---We support passing in adhoc filters for an analysis that don't live on the metric itself. These are in addition to the metric's filters. To use this, you can pass in an array of Fact Table Filter Ids.
---@alias growthbook.PostFactMetricAnalysisRequestAdditionalNumeratorFiltersList string[]

---The type of population to analyze. Defaults to 'factTable', meaning the analysis will return the metric value for all units found in the fact table.
---@alias growthbook.PostFactMetricAnalysisRequestPopulationType "factTable"|"segment"

---@class growthbook.PostFactMetricAnalysisResponse
---@field metricAnalysis growthbook.MetricAnalysis

---@class growthbook.PostFactMetricRequest
---@field name string Short display name (e.g. `Purchases per user`). Put the definition in `description`.
---@field description? string Markdown. Put context here, not in the name.
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization.
---@field projects? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestProjectsList
---@field tags? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestTagsList Tags for filtering and grouping. Use these instead of encoding groups in names.
---@field metricType growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestMetricType|string
---@field numerator? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestNumerator|distilled.Null
---@field denominator? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestDenominator Only when metricType is 'ratio'
---@field inverse? boolean Set to true for things like Bounce Rate, where you want the metric to decrease
---@field quantileSettings? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestQuantileSettings Controls the settings for quantile metrics (mandatory if metricType is "quantile")
---@field funnelSettings? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestFunnelSettings Funnel metric settings (required when metricType is "funnel")
---@field cappingSettings? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestCappingSettings Upper cap. Omit on update to preserve it. Use type: none to disable it explicitly. Invalid values are rejected.
---@field lowerCappingSettings? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestLowerCappingSettings|distilled.Null Independent lower cap. Omit on update to preserve it. Use null or type: none to disable it explicitly. Invalid values are rejected. For mixed cap types, the absolute bound takes precedence if thresholds cross.
---@field windowSettings? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestWindowSettings Controls the conversion window for the metric
---@field priorSettings? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestPriorSettings Controls the bayesian prior for the metric. If omitted, organization defaults will be used.
---@field regressionAdjustmentSettings? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestRegressionAdjustmentSettings Controls the regression adjustment (CUPED) settings for the metric
---@field riskThresholdSuccess? number No longer used. Accepted and ignored.
---@field riskThresholdDanger? number No longer used. Accepted and ignored.
---@field displayAsPercentage? boolean If true and the metric is a ratio or dailyParticipation metric, variation means will be displayed as a percentage. Defaults to true for dailyParticipation metrics and false for ratio metrics.
---@field minPercentChange? number Minimum percent change to consider uplift significant, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.005 for 0.5%)
---@field maxPercentChange? number Maximum percent change to consider uplift significant, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.5 for 50%)
---@field minSampleSize? number
---@field targetMDE? number The percentage change that you want to reliably detect before ending an experiment, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.1 for 10%). This is used to estimate the "Days Left" for running experiments.
---@field managedBy? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestManagedBy|string Set this to "api" (or "dbt" for resources synced from dbt) to disable editing in the GrowthBook UI
---@field metricAutoSlices? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestMetricAutoSlicesList Array of slice column names that will be automatically included in metric analysis. This is an enterprise feature.
---@field replaces? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestReplacesList Ids of older metrics (legacy or fact) that this metric supersedes, for example the legacy metric it was migrated from. Cannot include this metric's own id. Informational only - GrowthBook uses it to link the old and new definitions in the UI and to keep showing results from a snapshot that was created before an experiment switched to this metric. This field can only be set through the API.

---Upper cap. Omit on update to preserve it. Use type: none to disable it explicitly. Invalid values are rejected.
---@class growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestCappingSettings
---@field type growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestCappingSettingsType|string
---@field value? number When type is absolute, this must be a finite number greater than zero. When type is percentile, this must be strictly between 0 and 1. Required when enabling capping or changing type; omitted values are preserved only for same-type updates.
---@field ignoreZeros? boolean If true and capping is `percentile`, zeros will be ignored when calculating the percentile.

---@alias growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestCappingSettingsType "none"|"absolute"|"percentile"

---Only when metricType is 'ratio'
---@class growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestDenominator
---@field factTableId string
---@field column string The column name or one of the special values: '$$distinctUsers' or '$$count' (or '$$distinctDates' if metricType is 'mean' or 'ratio' or 'quantile' and quantileSettings.type is 'unit')
---@field aggregation? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestDenominatorAggregation|string User aggregation of selected column. Either sum or max for numeric columns; count distinct for string columns; hll merge / kll merge for pre-built sketch columns (requires data-source support); ignored for special columns. Default: sum. If you specify a string column you must explicitly specify count distinct. Not used for proportion metrics; for event quantile metrics only kll merge is applicable.
---@field filters? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestDenominatorFiltersList Array of Fact Table Filter Ids. Deprecated, use rowFilters instead.
---@field inlineFilters? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestDenominatorInlineFiltersMap Inline filters to apply to the fact table. Keys are column names, values are arrays of values to filter by. Deprecated, use rowFilters instead.
---@field rowFilters? growthbook.PostFactMetricRequestDenominatorRowFiltersList Filters to apply to the rows of the fact table before aggregation.

---User aggregation of selected column. Either sum or max for numeric columns; count distinct for string columns; hll merge / kll merge for pre-built sketch columns (requires data-source support); ignored for special columns. Default: sum. If you specify a string column you must explicitly specify count distinct. Not used for proportion metrics; for event quantile metrics only kll merge is applicable.
