---@class growthbook.PostFeatureV2Request
---@field skipSchemaValidation? growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestSkipSchemaValidation Deprecated — pass `skipSchemaValidation` in the request body instead.
---@field ignoreWarnings? growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestIgnoreWarnings Deprecated — pass `ignoreWarnings` in the request body instead.
---@field id string Unique, permanent key, shown as the Feature Flag's name in the UI and used in code. Keep it short. If `featureRegexValidator` in `GET /api/v1/settings` is set, follow it (`featureKeyExample` shows the format); otherwise use kebab-case (e.g. `checkout-express-pay`). Put context in `description`.
---@field archived? boolean
---@field description? string Markdown. What the Feature Flag gates and why, rollout plan, and links. Put context here, not in the key.
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization. When omitted, it defaults to the requesting member: a personal access token's owner, or the member an organization API key assumes. An organization API key acting as itself must send it, or the request fails with a 400.
---@field project? string An associated project ID
---@field targetingAllProjects? boolean Make this feature discoverable in — and served to — every project, beyond its primary `project`. Requires the `targetFeatures` permission (FlagsTarget policy) unscoped to any project. Governance stays with `project`.
---@field targetingProjects? growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestTargetingProjectsList Secondary project IDs this feature is targeted in and served to, beyond its primary `project`. Adding a project requires the `targetFeatures` permission (FlagsTarget policy) in that project. Governance stays with `project`.
---@field valueType growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestValueType|string The data type of the feature payload. Boolean by default.
---@field defaultValue string Default value when feature is enabled. Type must match `valueType`. In Config mode (`baseConfig` set) the default must be exactly a config with no overrides: send `"{}"` to use `baseConfig`, or set `defaultValueConfig` to point at a descendant.
---@field baseConfig? string|distilled.Null Key of the config backing this flag ("Config mode"). Requires `valueType: "json"` and a live config. The config supplies the base JSON and schema; `defaultValue` and rule values are override patches on top. null or omitted for a plain flag.
---@field defaultValueConfig? string|distilled.Null Optional. A config within `baseConfig`'s family that the default value resolves to instead of `baseConfig` itself. null or omitted means the default is `baseConfig`. The default is exactly this config and carries no overrides of its own.
---@field tags? growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestTagsList Tags for filtering and grouping. Use these instead of encoding groups in names.
---@field rules? growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestRulesList Feature rules. Each rule carries its own environment scope via `allEnvironments` / `environments`.
---@field environments? growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestEnvironmentsMap Per-environment enabled state, keyed by environment ID. An environment you leave out uses its "Default state for new features" setting, which may be enabled. To create the Feature Flag disabled, list every environment with `enabled: false`. Rules go on the top-level `rules` field.
---@field prerequisites? growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestPrerequisitesList Feature IDs. Each feature must evaluate to `true`
---@field jsonSchema? string Use JSON schema to validate the payload of a JSON-type feature value (enterprise only).
---@field customFields? growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestCustomFieldsMap
---@field comment? string Comment to record on the feature's initial revision. Defaults to an empty comment.
---@field skipHooks? boolean Set to true to publish despite a Custom Hook rejection. This does not bypass schema validation; use `skipSchemaValidation` for that. The caller must have Bypass draft approvals access for Feature Flags, Configs, and Constants in every Project. Otherwise, this field is ignored. Only set this when a person has explicitly asked you to. If a check blocks you, stop and ask a person instead of working around it.
---@field allowUnscopedRules? boolean When the organization requires rules to target specific environments or Projects, set to true to save a rule that applies to All Environments and All Projects. Only set this when a person has explicitly asked you to. If a check blocks you, stop and ask a person instead of working around it.

---@alias growthbook.PostFeatureV2RequestCustomFieldsMap { [string]: string }

