---@class growthbook.PostMetricRequest
---@field datasourceId string ID for the [DataSource](#tag/DataSource_model)
---@field managedBy? growthbook.PostMetricRequestManagedBy|string Where this metric must be managed from. If not set (empty string), it can be managed from anywhere. If set to "api", it can be managed via the API only.
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization.
---@field name string Short display name (e.g. `Purchases per user`). Put the definition in `description`.
---@field description? string Markdown. Put context here, not in the name.
---@field type growthbook.PostMetricRequestType|string Type of metric. See [Metrics documentation](/app/metrics/legacy)
---@field tags? growthbook.PostMetricRequestTagsList Tags for filtering and grouping. Use these instead of encoding groups in names.
---@field projects? growthbook.PostMetricRequestProjectsList List of project IDs for projects that can access this metric
---@field archived? boolean
---@field behavior? growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehavior
---@field sql? growthbook.PostMetricRequestSql Preferred way to define SQL. Only one of `sql`, `sqlBuilder` or `mixpanel` allowed, and at least one must be specified.
---@field sqlBuilder? growthbook.PostMetricRequestSqlBuilder An alternative way to specify a SQL metric, rather than a full query. Using `sql` is preferred to `sqlBuilder`. Only one of `sql`, `sqlBuilder` or `mixpanel` allowed, and at least one must be specified.
---@field mixpanel? growthbook.PostMetricRequestMixpanel Only use for MixPanel (non-SQL) Data Sources. Only one of `sql`, `sqlBuilder` or `mixpanel` allowed, and at least one must be specified.

---@class growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehavior
---@field goal? growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorGoal|string
---@field cappingSettings? growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorCappingSettings Controls how outliers are handled
---@field cap? number (deprecated, use cappingSettings instead) This should be non-negative
---@field capping? growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorCapping|string|distilled.Null (deprecated, use cappingSettings instead) Used in conjunction with `capValue` to set the capping (winsorization). Do not specify or set to null for no capping. "absolute" will cap user values at the `capValue` if it is greater than 0. "percentile" will cap user values at the percentile of user values in an experiment using the `capValue` for the percentile, if greater than 0. <br/> If `behavior.capping` is non-null, you must specify `behavior.capValue`.
---@field capValue? number (deprecated, use cappingSettings instead) This should be non-negative. <br/> Must specify `behavior.capping` when setting `behavior.capValue`.
---@field windowSettings? growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorWindowSettings Controls the conversion window for the metric
---@field conversionWindowStart? number The start of a Conversion Window relative to the exposure date, in hours. This is equivalent to the [Conversion Delay](/app/metrics/legacy/#conversion-delay). <br/> Must specify both `behavior.conversionWindowStart` and `behavior.conversionWindowEnd` or neither.
---@field conversionWindowEnd? number The end of a [Conversion Window](/app/metrics/legacy/#conversion-window) relative to the exposure date, in hours. This is equivalent to the [Conversion Delay](/app/metrics/legacy/#conversion-delay) + Conversion Window Hours settings in the UI. In other words, if you want a 48 hour window starting after 24 hours, you would set conversionWindowStart to 24 and conversionWindowEnd to 72 (24+48). <br/> Must specify both `behavior.conversionWindowStart` and `behavior.conversionWindowEnd` or neither.
---@field priorSettings? growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorPriorSettings Controls the bayesian prior for the metric. If omitted, organization defaults will be used.
---@field riskThresholdSuccess? number No longer used. Accepted and ignored.
---@field riskThresholdDanger? number No longer used. Accepted and ignored.
---@field minPercentChange? number Minimum percent change to consider uplift significant, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.005 for 0.5%)
---@field maxPercentChange? number Maximum percent change to consider uplift significant, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.5 for 50%)
---@field minSampleSize? number
---@field targetMDE? number The percentage change that you want to reliably detect before ending an experiment, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.1 for 10%). This is used to estimate the "Days Left" for running experiments.

---@alias growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorCapping "absolute"|"percentile"

---Controls how outliers are handled
---@class growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorCappingSettings
---@field type growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorCappingSettingsType|string|distilled.Null
---@field value? number When type is absolute, this is the absolute value. When type is percentile, this is the percentile value (from 0.0 to 1.0).
---@field ignoreZeros? boolean If true and capping is `percentile`, zeros will be ignored when calculating the percentile.

---@alias growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorCappingSettingsType "none"|"absolute"|"percentile"

---@alias growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorGoal "increase"|"decrease"

---Controls the bayesian prior for the metric. If omitted, organization defaults will be used.
---@class growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorPriorSettings
---@field override boolean If false, the organization default settings will be used instead of the other settings in this object
---@field proper boolean If true, the `mean` and `stddev` will be used, otherwise we will use an improper flat prior.
---@field mean number The mean of the prior distribution of relative effects in proportion terms (e.g. 0.01 is 1%)
---@field stddev number Must be > 0. The standard deviation of the prior distribution of relative effects in proportion terms.

---Controls the conversion window for the metric
---@class growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorWindowSettings
---@field type growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorWindowSettingsType|string
---@field delayHours? number Wait this many hours after experiment exposure before counting conversions. Ignored if delayValue is set.
---@field delayValue? number Wait this long after experiment exposure before counting conversions.
---@field delayUnit? growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorWindowSettingsDelayUnit|string Default `hours`.
---@field windowValue? number
---@field windowUnit? growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorWindowSettingsWindowUnit|string

---Default `hours`.
---@alias growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorWindowSettingsDelayUnit "minutes"|"hours"|"days"|"weeks"

---@alias growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorWindowSettingsType "none"|"conversion"|"lookback"

---@alias growthbook.PostMetricRequestBehaviorWindowSettingsWindowUnit "minutes"|"hours"|"days"|"weeks"

---Where this metric must be managed from. If not set (empty string), it can be managed from anywhere. If set to "api", it can be managed via the API only.
---@alias growthbook.PostMetricRequestManagedBy ""|"api"

---Only use for MixPanel (non-SQL) Data Sources. Only one of `sql`, `sqlBuilder` or `mixpanel` allowed, and at least one must be specified.
