---@class growthbook.PutMetricRequest
---@field id string The id of the requested resource
---@field managedBy? growthbook.PutMetricRequestManagedBy|string Where this metric must be managed from. If not set (empty string), it can be managed from anywhere. If set to "api", it can be managed via the API only. Please note that we have deprecated support for setting the managedBy property to "admin". Your existing Legacy Metrics with this value will continue to work, but we suggest migrating to Fact Metrics instead.
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization.
---@field name? string Short display name (e.g. `Purchases per user`). Put the definition in `description`.
---@field description? string Markdown. Put context here, not in the name.
---@field type? growthbook.PutMetricRequestType|string Type of metric. See [Metrics documentation](/app/metrics/legacy)
---@field tags? growthbook.PutMetricRequestTagsList Tags for filtering and grouping. Use these instead of encoding groups in names.
---@field projects? growthbook.PutMetricRequestProjectsList List of project IDs for projects that can access this metric
---@field archived? boolean
---@field behavior? growthbook.PutMetricRequestBehavior
---@field sql? growthbook.PutMetricRequestSql Preferred way to define SQL. Only one of `sql`, `sqlBuilder` or `mixpanel` allowed.
---@field sqlBuilder? growthbook.PutMetricRequestSqlBuilder An alternative way to specify a SQL metric, rather than a full query. Using `sql` is preferred to `sqlBuilder`. Only one of `sql`, `sqlBuilder` or `mixpanel` allowed
---@field mixpanel? growthbook.PutMetricRequestMixpanel Only use for MixPanel (non-SQL) Data Sources. Only one of `sql`, `sqlBuilder` or `mixpanel` allowed.

---@class growthbook.PutMetricRequestBehavior
---@field goal? growthbook.PutMetricRequestBehaviorGoal|string
---@field cappingSettings? growthbook.PutMetricRequestBehaviorCappingSettings Controls how outliers are handled
---@field cap? number (deprecated, use cappingSettings instead) This should be non-negative
---@field capping? growthbook.PutMetricRequestBehaviorCapping|string|distilled.Null (deprecated, use cappingSettings instead) Used in conjunction with `capValue` to set the capping (winsorization). Do not specify or set to null for no capping. "absolute" will cap user values at the `capValue` if it is greater than 0. "percentile" will cap user values at the percentile of user values in an experiment using the `capValue` for the percentile, if greater than 0. <br/> If `behavior.capping` is non-null, you must specify `behavior.capValue`.
---@field capValue? number (deprecated, use cappingSettings instead) This should be non-negative. <br/> Must specify `behavior.capping` when setting `behavior.capValue`.
---@field windowSettings? growthbook.PutMetricRequestBehaviorWindowSettings Controls the conversion window for the metric
---@field conversionWindowStart? number The start of a Conversion Window relative to the exposure date, in hours. This is equivalent to the [Conversion Delay](/app/metrics/legacy/#conversion-delay). <br/> Must specify both `behavior.conversionWindowStart` and `behavior.conversionWindowEnd` or neither.
---@field conversionWindowEnd? number The end of a [Conversion Window](/app/metrics/legacy/#conversion-window) relative to the exposure date, in hours. This is equivalent to the [Conversion Delay](/app/metrics/legacy/#conversion-delay) + Conversion Window Hours settings in the UI. In other words, if you want a 48 hour window starting after 24 hours, you would set conversionWindowStart to 24 and conversionWindowEnd to 72 (24+48). <br/> Must specify both `behavior.conversionWindowStart` and `behavior.conversionWindowEnd` or neither.
---@field priorSettings? growthbook.PutMetricRequestBehaviorPriorSettings Controls the bayesian prior for the metric. If omitted, organization defaults will be used.
---@field riskThresholdSuccess? number No longer used. Accepted and ignored.
---@field riskThresholdDanger? number No longer used. Accepted and ignored.
---@field minPercentChange? number Minimum percent change to consider uplift significant, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.005 for 0.5%)
---@field maxPercentChange? number Maximum percent change to consider uplift significant, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.5 for 50%)
---@field minSampleSize? number
---@field targetMDE? number The percentage change that you want to reliably detect before ending an experiment, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.1 for 10%). This is used to estimate the "Days Left" for running experiments.

---@alias growthbook.PutMetricRequestBehaviorCapping "absolute"|"percentile"

