---@class growthbook.RampSchedule
---@field id string Unique identifier (rs_ prefix)
---@field dateCreated string
---@field dateUpdated string
---@field name string
---@field entityType growthbook.RampScheduleEntityType
---@field entityId string
---@field targets growthbook.RampScheduleTargetsList Controlled entity references
---@field startActions? growthbook.RampScheduleStartActionsList Actions that restore controlled rules to their pre-ramp state. Applied when rolling back or jumping to start, and the base every step accumulates on; the only place a plan can set hashAttribute, seed or hashVersion.
---@field steps growthbook.RampScheduleStepsList Ordered ramp steps
---@field endActions? growthbook.RampScheduleEndActionsList Actions applied on top of all step patches when the ramp completes. Represents the final desired rule state.
---@field startDate? string|distilled.Null When the ramp fires. Absent/null means immediately on publish; set to a future datetime to delay start and keep the rule disabled until that time.
---@field cutoffDate? string|distilled.Null Rule-level kill date. When reached, the ramp is completed and the rule is disabled (enabled=false). Use for time-boxed rules that must stop serving on a fixed date regardless of ramp progress. Set to null to clear.
---@field requiresStartApproval? boolean When true, the ramp holds at step -1 with its rule disabled (zero traffic) until a human approves the start via /actions/approve-step. Composes with startDate ('hold until approved, then arm for that date').
---@field startApprovedAt? string|distilled.Null When the current launch's start was approved. Cleared on every return to step -1 (publish, rollback), re-arming the approval gate.
---@field status growthbook.RampScheduleStatus
---@field currentStepIndex number Index of current step; -1 = not yet started
---@field startedAt? string|distilled.Null
---@field phaseStartedAt? string|distilled.Null Anchor for cumulative interval timing; resets after each approval gate is satisfied
---@field pausedAt? string|distilled.Null
---@field nextStepAt string|distilled.Null When the current step's time gate elapses; null for steps with no interval (pure approval gates) and terminal states
---@field nextProcessAt? string|distilled.Null
---@field elapsedMs? number|distilled.Null Milliseconds since startedAt (computed at response time, not stored)
---@field lockdownConfig? growthbook.RampScheduleLockdownConfig
---@field monitoringConfig? growthbook.RampScheduleMonitoringConfig|distilled.Null
---@field experimentHealthAction? growthbook.RampScheduleExperimentHealthAction
---@field currentStepEnteredAt? string|distilled.Null
---@field stepApproval? growthbook.RampScheduleStepApproval|distilled.Null Approval record for the current step. Valid only while `stepApproval.stepIndex === currentStepIndex`.
---@field awaitingApproval boolean Computed at read time: whether a human approval is the gate blocking the schedule right now — either the start-approval gate (`requiresStartApproval` before step 0) or the current step's `holdConditions.requiresApproval` once its time hold (if any) has elapsed. Paused schedules report `false` (the pause is the blocking gate). For monitored steps the approve-step endpoint may still reject an approval until analysis-based gates clear.
---@field monitoringStartDate? string|distilled.Null When the monitored section most recently started (first monitored step entered). Used for no-traffic grace period gating.
---@field lastRollbackAt? string|distilled.Null
---@field lastRollbackReason? string|distilled.Null
---@field monitoringStatus? growthbook.RampScheduleMonitoringStatus|distilled.Null Read-only monitoring status. Present when monitoringConfig is set.

---@class growthbook.RampScheduleEndActionsItem
---@field targetType string
---@field targetId string
---@field patch growthbook.RampScheduleEndActionsItemPatch

---@class growthbook.RampScheduleEndActionsItemPatch
---@field ruleId string
---@field coverage? number|distilled.Null Traffic fraction (0–1). For monitored steps the rollout rule is promoted to an experiment: treatment = [0, coverage), control = [0.5, 0.5+coverage). Both arms are equal-sized and non-adjacent, so a step-up only adds new users to each arm — no existing user changes group. The REST API enforces coverage ≤ 0.5 on monitored steps so control end never exceeds 1.0. The SDK uses explicit hash ranges on bucketingV2 clients to keep bucketing stable across monitored/unmonitored transitions.
---@field condition? string|distilled.Null
---@field savedGroups? growthbook.RampScheduleEndActionsItemPatchSavedGroupsList|distilled.Null
---@field prerequisites? growthbook.RampScheduleEndActionsItemPatchPrerequisitesList|distilled.Null
---@field allEnvironments? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field environments? growthbook.RampScheduleEndActionsItemPatchEnvironmentsList|distilled.Null
