---@class growthbook.UpdateConfigRequest
---@field key string The key of the config
---@field skipSchemaValidation? growthbook.UpdateConfigRequestSkipSchemaValidation Deprecated — pass `skipSchemaValidation` in the request body instead.
---@field ignoreWarnings? growthbook.UpdateConfigRequestIgnoreWarnings Deprecated — pass `ignoreWarnings` in the request body instead.
---@field name? string Short display name. Put details in `description`.
---@field parent? string Change the lineage parent (the `key` of the config to inherit from). Set to an empty string to detach from the parent and make this a root config.
---@field extends? growthbook.UpdateConfigRequestExtendsList Replace the composition bases (mixins) layered on top of `parent`, in precedence order (later overrides earlier; all override `parent`; own keys win last). Send the complete set; an empty array clears all mixins. Set inheritance here, never via a `@config:` entry in `value`.
---@field value? growthbook.UpdateConfigRequestValueMap This config's base value as a JSON object. Per-environment/project variants are expressed via `scopedOverrides`.
---@field scopedOverrides? growthbook.UpdateConfigRequestScopedOverridesList Replace the ordered, first-match-wins environment/project-scoped variant selection. Each entry points at a flavor config (a child config, by `key`) whose value is deep-merged onto this config's resolved value when the (environment, project) scope matches. Send the complete list; an empty array clears all overrides; omit to leave unchanged. Entries must reference existing configs, may not reference this config itself, and may not be unreachable.
---@field description? string Markdown. Put context here, not in the name.
---@field project? string
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization.
---@field schema? growthbook.ConfigSchemaSource Replace this config's field definitions, as a JSON Schema document (`{ type: "json-schema", value }`) or typed-code source (`{ type: "typescript" | "protobuf" | "python" | "go" | "rust", value }`). Fields whose key a published ancestor already owns follow "base wins": an identical re-declaration is stripped with a `redundant-declaration` warning; one with a differing definition is rejected. A schema change cascades the 'base wins' normalization to descendants when published; a change that removes or retypes fields descendants still use soft-blocks with a 422 unless the request body sets `ignoreWarnings: true`. Conversion warnings are returned in `warnings`.
---@field source? string Optional identifier of the consuming codebase/service. When a `typescript` or `protobuf` schema is supplied, its named-type structure is captured under this source for reproduction on export.
---@field extensible? boolean
---@field experimentGuard? boolean Enable or disable the experiment guard for this Config. Disabling it requires Bypass draft approvals access.
---@field invariants? growthbook.UpdateConfigRequestInvariantsList Replace the config's cross-field validation rules. Each rule's expression is a mongo condition (mongrule). Send the complete set; an empty array clears all rules. Omit to leave them unchanged.
---@field bypassApproval? boolean Set to true to write directly to the live Config without approval. The caller must have Bypass draft approvals access in the Config's Project, unless the organization enables the REST API approval bypass. This field has no effect when approval is not required.
---@field skipHooks? boolean Set to true to publish despite a Custom Hook rejection. This does not bypass schema validation; use `skipSchemaValidation` for that. The caller must have Bypass draft approvals access for Feature Flags, Configs, and Constants in every Project. Otherwise, this field is ignored. Only set this when a person has explicitly asked you to. If a check blocks you, stop and ask a person instead of working around it.

---Replace the composition bases (mixins) layered on top of `parent`, in precedence order (later overrides earlier; all override `parent`; own keys win last). Send the complete set; an empty array clears all mixins. Set inheritance here, never via a `@config:` entry in `value`.
---@alias growthbook.UpdateConfigRequestExtendsList string[]

---Deprecated — pass `ignoreWarnings` in the request body instead.
---@alias growthbook.UpdateConfigRequestIgnoreWarnings string|boolean

