---@class growthbook.UpdateDimensionRequest
---@field id string The id of the requested resource
---@field name? string Short display name. Put details in `description`.
---@field description? string Description of the dimension
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization.
---@field datasourceId? string ID of the datasource this dimension belongs to
---@field identifierType? string Type of identifier (user, anonymous, etc.)
---@field query? string SQL query or equivalent for the dimension
---@field managedBy? growthbook.UpdateDimensionRequestManagedBy|string Where this dimension must be managed from. If not set (empty string), it can be managed from anywhere.

---Where this dimension must be managed from. If not set (empty string), it can be managed from anywhere.
---@alias growthbook.UpdateDimensionRequestManagedBy ""|"api"

---@class growthbook.UpdateDimensionResponse
---@field dimension growthbook.Dimension

---@class growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequest
---@field id string The id of the requested resource
---@field datasourceId? string Changing it needs an `assignmentQueryId` from the new one, and drops the metrics, segment and unit dimensions that aren't from it.
---@field assignmentQuery? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestAssignmentQuery The assignment query, grouping its ID with the identifier type analyzed on. Mutually exclusive with the deprecated `assignmentQueryId`.
---@field assignmentQueryId? string Deprecated: use `assignmentQuery`. Rejected when selecting a different assignment query that declares several identifier types; set `assignmentQuery.identifierType` instead.
---@field isClusterExperiment? boolean Run as a cluster-randomized experiment: randomize on the assignment query's identifier type (the cluster, e.g. region_id) while analyzing a nested sub-unit (clusterSubUnitIdentifier, e.g. user_id). The assignment query must declare both identifier types.
---@field clusterSubUnitIdentifier? string The nested sub-unit identifier type analyzed within each cluster (e.g. user_id). Required when isClusterExperiment is true; must be declared by the assignment query and differ from its cluster identifier type.
---@field trackingKey? string Key sent with exposure events. Keep it short, in kebab-case (usually the Feature Flag key). If your organization requires a tracking key format, a key that doesn't match is rejected with `invalid_tracking_key`. Changing it after launch splits exposures across two keys.
---@field bypassDuplicateKeyCheck? boolean If true, allow updating the tracking key even if another experiment with the same tracking key already exist. This is ignored if the organization requires unique tracking keys as a rule. Only set this when a person has explicitly asked you to. If a check blocks you, stop and ask a person instead of working around it.
---@field name? string Short display name (e.g. `Express checkout button`). Put reasoning in `hypothesis` and context in `description`.
---@field type? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestType|string
---@field bypassApproval? boolean Deprecated and ignored. Approval is bypassed automatically when the caller has Bypass draft approvals access for this resource or when the organization enables the REST API approval bypass. Otherwise, the revision must be approved before it can be published.
---@field project? string Project ID which the experiment belongs to
---@field hypothesis? string Markdown. If we change X, metric Y will move because Z.
---@field description? string Markdown. Put context here, not in the name.
---@field tags? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestTagsList Tags for filtering and grouping. Use these instead of encoding groups in names.
---@field metrics? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestMetricsList
---@field secondaryMetrics? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestSecondaryMetricsList
---@field guardrailMetrics? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestGuardrailMetricsList
---@field activationMetric? string Users must convert on this metric before being included
---@field segmentId? string Only users in this segment will be included
---@field queryFilter? string WHERE clause to add to the default experiment query
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization.
---@field archived? boolean
---@field linkedChanges? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestLinkedChanges|string Required while the experiment still serves through linked changes. "materialize" keeps a stopped experiment's released variation as a permanent force rule on each linked Feature Flag; "remove" acknowledges that the linked changes stop serving.
---@field status? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestStatus|string
---@field autoRefresh? boolean
---@field hashAttribute? string
---@field fallbackAttribute? string
---@field attributeScopeAllProjects? boolean Picker preference: show attributes from all projects in this experiment's targeting UI instead of only those in scope for its project and linked features. Does not loosen enforcement — when the organization requires registered attributes with project scoping, out-of-scope attributes are still rejected.
---@field hashVersion? number
---@field disableStickyBucketing? boolean
---@field bucketVersion? number
---@field minBucketVersion? number
---@field results? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestResults|string The result status of the experiment. Maps to resultSummary.status in the GET response.
---@field winner? number The index of the winning variation (0-indexed). Maps to resultSummary.winner (variation ID) in the GET response.
---@field analysis? string Analysis summary or conclusions for the experiment. Maps to resultSummary.conclusions in the GET response.
---@field releasedVariationId? string The ID of the released variation. Maps to resultSummary.releasedVariationId in the GET response.
---@field excludeFromPayload? boolean If true, the experiment is excluded from the SDK payload. Maps to resultSummary.excludeFromPayload in the GET response.
---@field inProgressConversions? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestInProgressConversions|string
---@field attributionModel? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestAttributionModel|string Setting attribution model to `"experimentDuration"` is the same as selecting "Ignore Conversion Windows" for the Conversion Window Override. Setting it to `"lookbackOverride"` requires a `lookbackOverride` object to be provided.
---@field lookbackOverride? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestLookbackOverride Controls the lookback override for the experiment. For type "window", value must be a non-negative number and valueUnit is required.
---@field statsEngine? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestStatsEngine|string
---@field variations? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestVariationsList
---@field phases? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestPhasesList
---@field regressionAdjustmentEnabled? boolean Controls whether regression adjustment (CUPED) is enabled for experiment analyses
---@field sequentialTestingEnabled? boolean Only applicable to frequentist analyses
---@field sequentialTestingTuningParameter? number
---@field shareLevel? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestShareLevel|string
---@field banditScheduleValue? number
---@field banditScheduleUnit? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestBanditScheduleUnit|string
---@field banditBurnInValue? number
---@field banditBurnInUnit? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestBanditBurnInUnit|string
---@field banditConversionWindowValue? number
---@field banditConversionWindowUnit? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestBanditConversionWindowUnit|string
---@field postStratificationEnabled? boolean|distilled.Null When null, the organization default is used.
---@field decisionFrameworkSettings? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestDecisionFrameworkSettings Controls the decision framework and metric overrides for the experiment. Replaces the entire stored object on update (does not patch individual fields).
---@field metricOverrides? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestMetricOverridesList Per-metric analysis overrides for this experiment. Replaces the entire stored array (does not patch individual entries).
---@field defaultDashboardId? string ID of the default dashboard for this experiment.
---@field customFields? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestCustomFieldsMap
---@field customMetricSlices? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestCustomMetricSlicesList Custom slices that apply to ALL applicable metrics in the experiment
---@field statusUpdateSchedule? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestStatusUpdateSchedule|distilled.Null
---@field precomputedUnitDimensionIds? growthbook.UpdateExperimentRequestPrecomputedUnitDimensionIdsList
---@field ignoreWarnings? boolean Set to true to acknowledge the warnings listed in a blocked response and continue. This covers experiment guards, locked dependents, and references affected by an archive. When the organization treats schema failures as warnings, it also covers schema and invariant warnings. It never bypasses a rejected Custom Hook. On revision publish endpoints, it can also force-publish an out-of-date draft when the caller has Bypass draft approvals access. Only set this when a person has explicitly asked you to. If a check blocks you, stop and ask a person instead of working around it.
---@field skipChecklist? boolean When `status` starts a draft: start past its incomplete launch checklist items, as `POST /experiments/{id}/start` does. Only set this when a person has explicitly asked you to. If a check blocks you, stop and ask a person instead of working around it.

