---@class growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequest
---@field id string The id of the requested resource
---@field name? string Short display name (e.g. `Purchases per user`). Put the definition in `description`.
---@field description? string Markdown. Put context here, not in the name.
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization.
---@field projects? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestProjectsList
---@field tags? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestTagsList Tags for filtering and grouping. Use these instead of encoding groups in names.
---@field metricType? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestMetricType|string
---@field numerator? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestNumerator|distilled.Null
---@field denominator? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestDenominator Only when metricType is 'ratio'
---@field inverse? boolean Set to true for things like Bounce Rate, where you want the metric to decrease
---@field quantileSettings? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestQuantileSettings Controls the settings for quantile metrics (mandatory if metricType is "quantile")
---@field funnelSettings? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestFunnelSettings Funnel metric settings (required when metricType is "funnel")
---@field cappingSettings? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestCappingSettings Upper cap. Omit on update to preserve it. Use type: none to disable it explicitly. Invalid values are rejected.
---@field lowerCappingSettings? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestLowerCappingSettings|distilled.Null Independent lower cap. Omit on update to preserve it. Use null or type: none to disable it explicitly. Invalid values are rejected. For mixed cap types, the absolute bound takes precedence if thresholds cross.
---@field windowSettings? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestWindowSettings Controls the conversion window for the metric
---@field priorSettings? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestPriorSettings Controls the bayesian prior for the metric. If omitted, organization defaults will be used.
---@field regressionAdjustmentSettings? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestRegressionAdjustmentSettings Controls the regression adjustment (CUPED) settings for the metric
---@field riskThresholdSuccess? number No longer used. Accepted and ignored.
---@field riskThresholdDanger? number No longer used. Accepted and ignored.
---@field displayAsPercentage? boolean If true and the metric is a ratio or dailyParticipation metric, variation means will be displayed as a percentage. Defaults to true for dailyParticipation metrics and false for ratio metrics.
---@field minPercentChange? number Minimum percent change to consider uplift significant, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.005 for 0.5%)
---@field maxPercentChange? number Maximum percent change to consider uplift significant, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.5 for 50%)
---@field minSampleSize? number
---@field targetMDE? number The percentage change that you want to reliably detect before ending an experiment, as a proportion (e.g. put 0.1 for 10%). This is used to estimate the "Days Left" for running experiments.
---@field managedBy? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestManagedBy|string Set this to "api" (or "dbt" for resources synced from dbt) to disable editing in the GrowthBook UI
---@field metricAutoSlices? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestMetricAutoSlicesList Array of slice column names that will be automatically included in metric analysis. This is an enterprise feature.
---@field replaces? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestReplacesList Ids of older metrics (legacy or fact) that this metric supersedes, for example the legacy metric it was migrated from. Cannot include this metric's own id. Informational only - GrowthBook uses it to link the old and new definitions in the UI and to keep showing results from a snapshot that was created before an experiment switched to this metric. This field can only be set through the API.
---@field archived? boolean Set to true to archive the metric. Archived metrics are hidden by default in the UI and excluded from new experiments.

---Upper cap. Omit on update to preserve it. Use type: none to disable it explicitly. Invalid values are rejected.
---@class growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestCappingSettings
---@field type growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestCappingSettingsType|string
---@field value? number When type is absolute, this must be a finite number greater than zero. When type is percentile, this must be strictly between 0 and 1. Required when enabling capping or changing type; omitted values are preserved only for same-type updates.
---@field ignoreZeros? boolean If true and capping is `percentile`, zeros will be ignored when calculating the percentile.

---@alias growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestCappingSettingsType "none"|"absolute"|"percentile"

---Only when metricType is 'ratio'
---@class growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestDenominator
---@field factTableId string
---@field column string The column name or one of the special values: '$$distinctUsers' or '$$count' (or '$$distinctDates' if metricType is 'mean' or 'ratio' or 'quantile' and quantileSettings.type is 'unit')
---@field aggregation? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestDenominatorAggregation|string User aggregation of selected column. Either sum or max for numeric columns; count distinct for string columns; hll merge / kll merge for pre-built sketch columns (requires data-source support); ignored for special columns. Default: sum. If you specify a string column you must explicitly specify count distinct. Not used for proportion metrics; for event quantile metrics only kll merge is applicable.
---@field filters? growthbook.UpdateFactMetricRequestDenominatorFiltersList Array of Fact Table Filter Ids. Deprecated, use rowFilters instead.
