---@class growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2Request
---@field id string The id of the requested resource
---@field skipSchemaValidation? growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestSkipSchemaValidation Deprecated — pass `skipSchemaValidation` in the request body instead.
---@field ignoreWarnings? growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestIgnoreWarnings Deprecated — pass `ignoreWarnings` in the request body instead.
---@field description? string Markdown. What the Feature Flag gates and why, rollout plan, and links. Put context here, not in the key.
---@field archived? boolean
---@field project? string An associated project ID
---@field targetingAllProjects? boolean Make this feature discoverable in — and served to — every project, beyond its primary `project`. Requires the `targetFeatures` permission (FlagsTarget policy) unscoped to any project. Governance stays with `project`.
---@field targetingProjects? growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestTargetingProjectsList Secondary project IDs this feature is targeted in and served to, beyond its primary `project`. Adding a project requires the `targetFeatures` permission (FlagsTarget policy) in that project. Governance stays with `project`.
---@field owner? string The userId or email address of the owner. If an email address is provided, it will be used to look up the userId of the matching organization member. If an ID is provided, it will be validated as existing in the organization.
---@field defaultValue? string
---@field baseConfig? string|distilled.Null The config backing this flag, fixed at creation. Cannot be changed by an update — resend the current value or omit it; a different value is rejected.
---@field defaultValueConfig? string|distilled.Null Optional. A config within `baseConfig`'s family that the default value resolves to instead of `baseConfig` itself. null or omitted means the default is `baseConfig`. The default is exactly this config and carries no overrides of its own.
---@field tags? growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestTagsList Tags for filtering and grouping. Use these instead of encoding groups in names. Replaces the existing tags completely.
---@field rules? growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestRulesList Replaces all feature rules atomically. Behavior differs from v1: v1 PUT applies per-environment patches, v2 PUT swaps the entire `rules` array in one revision. To preserve existing rules during a partial edit, GET the feature first, mutate the returned `rules` array, and PUT the full array back. Safe-rollout rules round-trip via their `safeRolloutId` (creation requires `POST /v2/features/:id/revisions/:version/rules`).
---@field environments? growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestEnvironmentsMap Per-environment enabled state. V2 rules are specified on the top-level `rules` field.
---@field prerequisites? growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestPrerequisitesList Feature IDs. Each feature must evaluate to `true`
---@field jsonSchema? string Use JSON schema to validate the payload of a JSON-type feature value (enterprise only).
---@field customFields? growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestCustomFieldsMap
---@field holdout? growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestHoldout|distilled.Null Holdout to assign this feature to. Pass `null` to remove the feature from its current holdout. Omit the field entirely to leave the holdout unchanged.
---@field comment? string Comment to record on the revision this update publishes, when it publishes one. Defaults to "Created via REST API".
---@field skipHooks? boolean Set to true to publish despite a Custom Hook rejection. This does not bypass schema validation; use `skipSchemaValidation` for that. The caller must have Bypass draft approvals access for Feature Flags, Configs, and Constants in every Project. Otherwise, this field is ignored. Only set this when a person has explicitly asked you to. If a check blocks you, stop and ask a person instead of working around it.
---@field allowUnscopedRules? boolean When the organization requires rules to target specific environments or Projects, set to true to save a rule that applies to All Environments and All Projects. Only set this when a person has explicitly asked you to. If a check blocks you, stop and ask a person instead of working around it.

---@alias growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestCustomFieldsMap { [string]: string }

---Per-environment enabled state. V2 rules are specified on the top-level `rules` field.
---@alias growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestEnvironmentsMap { [string]: growthbook.UpdateFeatureV2RequestEnvironmentsValue }

